(1924, 6, 'Introductoin to Parts of Speech', '', 49, '', '<h4><b>Word classes - slovnĂ­ druhy - parts of speech</b></a></h4>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>There are 10 word classes\r\nrecognized in the grammar of the Czech language:</p>\r\n<table border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0>\r\n <tr>\r\n <td width=227 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>1.<font size=1 face=\"Times New Roman\">Â Â Â Â Â  </i><b>Nouns</b></p>\r\n </td>\r\n <td width=132 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>podstatnĂĄ jmĂŠna</i></p>\r\n </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n <td width=227 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>2.<font size=1 face=\"Times New Roman\">Â Â Â Â Â  </i><b>Adjectives\r\n </b></p>\r\n </td>\r\n <td width=132 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>pĹĂ­davnĂĄ jmĂŠna</i></p>\r\n </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n <td width=227 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>3.<font size=1 face=\"Times New Roman\">Â Â Â Â Â  </i><b>Pronouns</b></p>\r\n </td>\r\n <td width=132 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>zĂĄjmena</i></p>\r\n </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n <td width=227 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>4.<font size=1 face=\"Times New Roman\">Â Â Â Â Â  </i><b>Numerals</b></p>\r\n </td>\r\n <td width=132 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>ÄĂ­slovky</i></p>\r\n </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n <td width=227 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>5.<font size=1 face=\"Times New Roman\">Â Â Â Â Â  </i><b>Verbs</b></p>\r\n </td>\r\n <td width=132 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>slovesa</i></p>\r\n </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n <td width=227 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>6.<font size=1 face=\"Times New Roman\">Â Â Â Â Â  </i><b>Adverbs</b></p>\r\n </td>\r\n <td width=132 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>pĹĂ­slovce</i></p>\r\n </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n <td width=227 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>7.<font size=1 face=\"Times New Roman\">Â Â Â Â Â  </i><b>Prepositions</b></p>\r\n </td>\r\n <td width=132 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>pĹedloÂky</i></p>\r\n </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n <td width=227 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>8.<font size=1 face=\"Times New Roman\">Â Â Â Â Â  </i><b>Conjunctions</b></p>\r\n </td>\r\n <td width=132 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>spojky</i></p>\r\n </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n <td width=227 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>9.<font size=1 face=\"Times New Roman\">Â Â Â Â Â  </i><b>Particles</b></p>\r\n </td>\r\n <td width=132 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>ÄĂĄstice</i></p>\r\n </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n <td width=227 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>10.<font size=1 face=\"Times New Roman\">Â  </i><b>Interjections</b></p>\r\n </td>\r\n <td width=132 valign=top>\r\n <p><i>citoslovce</i></p>\r\n </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>The first 5\r\nclasses change their form in different contexts. The changes in 1 Â 4 are\r\ncalled <i>declension</i>. The\r\nchanges in verbs (5) are called conjugation.</p>\r\n<p>Classes 6 Â 10 do not change\r\ntheir form (with one minor exception).</p>\r\n', 2, NULL),
