(929, 13, 'J', '', 'Ad %', '10% = desetiprocentnĂ­ (bez mezery)\r\n10 % = deset procent (s mezerou)\r\n\r\nPodobnÄ:\r\n50m = padesĂĄtimetrovĂ˝\r\n50 m = padesĂĄt metrĹŻ\r\n\r\nKdyÂ pĂ­Âu mezeru ve slovnĂ­m vyjĂĄdĹenĂ­, pĂ­Âe se takĂŠ ve znaÄce.\r\n\r\nVĂ˝jimkami jsou fyzikĂĄlnĂ­ jednotky teploty:\r\n50 Â°C = padesĂĄt stupĹĹŻ Celsia\r\n\r\na ĂşhlovĂŠ jednotky\r\n10Â° = deset stupĹĹŻ i desetistupĹovĂ˝', '2003-04-16 02:11:28', 8, 0),
(930, 13, 'J', '', 'Re: Does Hyrman Mean Anything?', 'Yes, HeĹman is derived from German Hermann.\r\nAnd heĹmĂĄnek is derived from HeĹman...', '2003-04-16 02:51:16', 569, 0),
(931, 13, 'J', '', 'Re: transgressive', 'You compared well: berouc = biorĹĄc = taking and minuvÂi = minĹĄwszy = having passed. The only difference is that in Polish the transgressives are commonly used in everyday speach, while in Czech they are considered realy archaic.\r\n\r\nI\'m not sure whether in Polish they change suffixes in masc./fem./neu. and sg./pl. In Czech they do.', '2003-04-16 03:08:40', 504, 0),
(932, 13, 'J', '', 'Re: stÄna vs. zeÄ', 'Technicaly \"stÄna\" means every vertical planar(2D) construction. \"ZeÄ\" is stÄna that is build of small elements like stones or bricks.', '2003-04-16 03:42:07', 97, 0),
(933, 13, 'Jerry Horna', 'jerry.horna@usa.net', 'Greeting Cards in the Czech Language', 'Where can someone in the USA purchase greeting cards printed in the Czech language?', '2003-04-16 22:48:41', 0, 0),
(934, 13, 'Scott', 'scott.brown@ilovejesus.net', 'Re: Greeting Cards in the Czech Language', 'Hi,\r\n\r\nI went to google.com and typed in \"Czech greeting cards\" and received tons of feedback.  I think the easiest way to find what you are looking for is to do the same.  I honestly think one of the only ways you will find them in America is on the internet. \r\n\r\nScott', '2003-04-17 00:43:33', 933, 0),
(935, 15, 'Shannon', 'odinhuxley@hotmail.com', 'Seeking Czech Teacher in Austin, Texas', 'I am looking for a Czech tutor in Austin, Texas. If you are one or know of one, please email me at: odinhuxley@hotmail.com', '2003-04-18 07:09:03', 0, 1),
