(937, 17, 'J', '', 'Velikonoce - The Easter', 'TĂŠma ke konverzaci mezi studenty (pĹĂ­padnÄ i uÄiteli):\r\n\r\nJak jste strĂĄvili Velikonoce. Co se VĂĄm nejvĂ­ce lĂ­bilo? Co VĂĄs nejvĂ­ce zaujalo na ÄeskĂ˝ch VelikonocĂ­ch? Jak slavĂ­te Velikonoce ve svĂŠ zemi?', '2003-04-21 22:13:01', 0, 0),
(938, 17, 'Erik Piper', 'erik@sky.cz', 'Re: Velikonoce - The Easter', 'Letos u kamarĂĄda - HolanÄana, kterĂ˝ Âije na moravskĂŠ venkovÄ, v SebranicĂ­ch. Âli jsme s manÂelkou a dcerou na prochĂĄzky, mezi prochĂĄzkami jsem se dĂ­val na Âvagra, jak hraje Lord of the Rings na Playstationu. Vstal jsem o VelikonocĂ­ch pozdÄ, protoÂe jsme se dĂ­vali na film Lord of the Rings dlouho do noci (vlastnÄ do velikonoÄnĂ­ho rĂĄna).\r\n\r\nSamozĹejmÄ jsem se povinnÄ musel uchopit mrskaÄky, ale stejnÄ jsem dostal od manÂelky vynadĂĄno za to, Âe to dÄlĂĄm moc lehce. \"NaÂtÄstĂ­\" kolovaly po vesnici i mistnĂ­ chlapi, kteĹĂ­ mrskali tak, jak se prĂ˝ mĂĄ. JeÂtÄ k tomu pouÂĂ­vali vÄtviÄky nÄjakĂŠho jehliÄnatĂŠho stromu - jahlovice??? nevĂ­m - aby to bylo ÂtĂ­plavÄjÂĂ­.\r\n\r\nNic \"velikonoÄnĂ­ho\" jsme neuvaĹili - najedli jsme se v motorestu - ale dcerka namalovala vajĂ­Äka a manÂelka pekla sladkĂ˝ chleba.\r\n\r\n\"Co VĂĄs nejvĂ­ce zaujalo na ÄeskĂ˝ch VelikonocĂ­ch?\" - asi uhadnete.\r\n\r\n\r\nJak slavĂ­te Velikonoce ve svĂŠ zemi? - NemĂĄm zemÄ svĂŠ.\r\nErik', '2003-04-23 16:16:11', 937, 1),
(939, 15, 'Scott', 'scott.brown@ilovejesus.net', 'PrĂĄci?', 'PromiĹte muj ÄeskĂ˝ protoÂe to je ÂpatnĂ˝, ale mĂĄm otĂĄzku.  Jak se Ĺekne AnglickĂ˝ prĂĄci? e.g. \"Kdy konÄiÂ zĂ­tra v prĂĄci?\" nebo \"ZaÄinĂĄte dneska v prĂĄci v 7 rĂĄno?\"\r\n\r\n\r\nCan you please correct any of my mistakes both with grammatics and sentence structure.\r\nTakĂŠ, jak se Ĺekne ÄeskĂ˝ \"can you please correct my mistakes\".  To je matoucĂ­ mÄ.\r\n\r\nDekuji,\r\nScott', '2003-04-24 01:02:58', 0, 0),
(940, 13, 'Penny', '', 'Need help translating', 'Need help translating some church records.  Cannot include the correct diacritics because of my american keyboard. \r\n Die 14 Nonem Cris(?) 1899 Sep elivi Marti nuni Rezac aesoctis 67 annoruni.\r\n\r\n Die 22 Decem Cris(?) 1899 Sysrlivi (or Syselivi) Annsini Rezac aetatis 58 annorum.\r\n \r\n Die 21 mensis Junii(?) A.D. 1908 Baptizavi Jaroslaum Aron Karpisek nat um die 17 mensis Junii(?) A.D. 1907.  ex Fransico Karpisek et Rosa Kavan. Patrini Fuerunt Antonius-Francisca Kriz.  Adnotationes: cioroliter juncti.\r\n\r\n Die 21 mensis Junii(?)A.D. 1908 baptizavi Albinum-Wenceslaum Kriz nat um die 1ma (ma is raised up) mensis Martii A.D. 1908 ex Antonio Kriz et Francisca n. Karpisek.  Patrini Fuerunt Wenceslaus et Agnes Kavan .  Thank you for your help.', '2003-04-24 03:26:54', 0, 1),
(941, 13, 'Erik Piper', 'erik@sky.cz', 'Re: Need help translating', 'Hello Penny,\r\n\r\nThese records are in Latin, not Czech. \r\n\r\n- I think \"Nonem Cris\" might actually be \"Novembris\", and thus November. Same with \"Decem Cris\". \r\n- \"anno...\" refers to years.\r\n- Marti nuni Rezac will probably by Martin ĹezĂĄÄ (or whatever - see old discussion), with a declension on the end - but I don\'t speak Latin, so I can\'t say which one. Likewise \"Ann\".\r\n- \"Baptizavi\" - something about baptism.\r\n- Patrini - most likely godparents.\r\n- ex... - most likely parents.\r\n- 1ma - 1st. 1ma mensis Martii - perhaps first week of March, although mensis sounds more like month.\r\n\r\nSorry I can\'t help more.\r\n', '2003-04-24 15:08:11', 940, 0),
(942, 15, 'Erik Piper', 'erik@sky.cz', 'Re: PrĂĄci?', 'I\'ll take a crack at it, though my Czech will certainly also contain mistakes.\r\n\r\nNejdĹĂ­v bych se chtÄl omluvit za svou Âpatnou ÄeÂtinu. Neotravil bych s nĂ­, ale mĂĄm otĂĄzku. Jak se anglicky Ĺekne \"prĂĄce\"? NapĹ. \"Kdy konÄĂ­Â zĂ­tra v prĂĄci\"? nebo \"Dneska zaÄĂ­nĂĄte v prĂĄci v 7 hodin rĂĄno\"?\r\n\r\n- Punctuation always follows quote marks in Czech\r\n- I\'m not bold enough to use the Czech for \"Excuse me... but...\" - it strongly feels like an <i>anglicismus</i> to me. Keep in mind that the opposition in \"but\" is very abstract in \"Excuse me... but...\" (it really means \"I regret that I am bothering you... but\"). I checked Google for instances of \"ale mĂĄm otĂĄzku\" and couldn\'t find an equivalent of the English idiom, so I chickened out and chose the \"polopatickĂŠ\" [1] solution above.\r\n   - overall - develop an ear for what\'s an idiom in English. If you think something is an idiom, say it in a roundabout way and keep your ears open for how the person speaking with you expresses the same notion.\r\n- Jak se (lang-adv) Ĺekne, not Jak se Ĺekne (lang-adj)\r\n- language adjectives are not capitalized\r\n- not sure why, but \"kdy zĂ­tra konÄĂ­Â...\" sounds more natural to me than \"kdy konÄĂ­Â zĂ­tra...\"\r\n- If I\'m any indication, then years of torture await you as you learn to hear, remember, and systematically think about long and short vowels, even though you\'re doing extremely well.\r\n\r\n\"can you please correct my mistakes\" - \r\n\"Mohl bych (TÄ/VĂĄs) poprosit, abys(te) mi opravil(a) chyby (v tomto dokumentu)?\"\r\n\r\nTo mÄ vÂdycky mate. \r\n(The structure \"That\'s xxxx-ing for me\" is pretty rare in Czech:\r\nThat\'s confusing for me - see above\r\nThat\'s frustrating for me - to je frustrujĂ­cĂ­\r\nThat\'s depressing for me - to mÄ deptĂĄ\r\nThat was pretty time-consuming for me - To mi trvalo dost dlouho.\r\n\r\n[1] polopatickĂ˝ - po + lopatÄ + ickĂ˝ - shovel-by-shovel + adj. - made painfully explicit and step-by-step, usually for reasons of dumbing-down (here more for reasons of my own dumbness). Often appears as an adverb (polopaticky).\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nErik', '2003-04-24 15:37:21', 939, 1),
(943, 15, 'Erik Piper', 'erik@sky.cz', 'Re: PrĂĄci?', 'Just a couple more notes - \r\n- watch out for cases where you need to use \"sv-\" and not a regular pronominal adjective (m-, va-, tv-, etc.). The key question here is: does it refer to the subject of the given clause? If so, use the reflexive \"sv-\".\r\n\r\nDĂĄl mi moje hodinky - \"He gave me my watch.\" \r\n   - Here, the subject of the given clause - the sentence\'s main clause, in other words, the sentence\'s subject - is \"he\", the adjective is \"my\": no problem\r\n\r\nMĂĄm s sebou hodinky svoje - \"I have <i>my</i> watch with me, not somebody else\'s.\"\r\n   - Here, the subject of the given clause is \"I\", the adjective is \"my\"; it thus refers back to the subject, and thus the reflexive \"svoje\" is needed.\r\n\r\nPromĂ­Ĺte mi moji Âpatnou ÄeÂtinu. OmlouvĂĄm se za svoji Âpatnou ÄeÂtinu. Omluvte, prosĂ­m, moji Âpatnou ÄeÂtinu.\r\n\r\n- I just realized that the advice \"Jak se (lang-adv) Ĺekne\" is a bit too strict - \"Jak se Ĺekne (lang-adv)\" is OK too. In fact, the latter has more hits on Google (although many are caused by a joke existing on multiple joke pages).', '2003-04-24 15:55:11', 942, 0),
(944, 15, 'Scott', 'scott.brown@ilovejesus.net', 'Re: PrĂĄci?', 'Thanks for all the help!  I just have two questions.  When saying \"OmlouvĂĄm\" or \"Omluvte\" what is the significance of the \'O\'.  I understand the place that it is taking, but when I look the word up I cannot find any root of this, nor have I anywhere else I have looked.  I would like to have a complete understanding of it.  Also, I really am curious about the question I asked.  What does \"PrĂĄci\" mean?  Does it mean work?  The way it is used in many sentences leads me to think yes, but I would like confirmation.  \r\n\r\nThe hardest part I am having with speaking or writing Czech is thinking how to structure the sentences.  It is so foreign to my thinking of English or Spanish.  It has some similarities to Spanish sentences, but is still much different.  I guess that is one of the hard points about any language.  Like you said, much practice and a lot of suffering will be the only solution.\r\n\r\nThanks Erik,\r\nScott', '2003-04-25 01:49:04', 943, 0),
(945, 13, 'VladimĂ­r', '', 'Re: Need help translating', 'Die 14 Nevembris 1899 sepelivi Martinum ĹezĂĄÄ aetatis 67 annorum.\r\nDie 22 Decembris 1899 sepelivi Annam ĹezĂĄÄ aetatis 58 annorum.\r\n\r\nDne 14. listopadu 1899 pohĹbil jsem Martina ĹezĂĄÄe ve vÄku 67 let.\r\nDne 22. prosince 1899 pohĹbil jsem Annu ĹezĂĄÄovou ve vÄku 58 let.', '2003-04-25 13:29:07', 940, 0),
(946, 13, 'VladimĂ­r', '', 'Re: Need help translating', '21. dne mÄsĂ­ce Äervna L.P. 1908 pokĹtil jsem Jaroslava Ărona KarpĂ­Âka nar. dne 17. Äervna 1907 z FrantiÂka KarpĂ­Âka a RĹŻÂeny KavanovĂŠ. Kmotry byli AntonĂ­n a FrantiÂka KĹĂ­Âovi. PoznĂĄmka: ? spojeni.\r\n\r\nDne 21. Äervna 1908 pokĹtil jsem AlbĂ­na VĂĄclava KĹĂ­Âe nar. 1. bĹezna 1908 z AntonĂ­na KĹĂ­Âe a FrantiÂky roz. KarpĂ­ÂkovĂŠ. Kmotry byli VĂĄclav a AneÂka Kavanovi.', '2003-04-25 13:47:33', 940, 0),
(947, 13, 'Erik Piper', 'erik@sky.cz', 'Re: Need help translating', 'On November 14th, 1899, I laid to rest Martin ĹezĂĄÄ at the age of 67 years.\r\nOn December 22nd, 1899, I laid to rest Anna ĹezĂĄÄovĂĄ at the age of 58 years.\r\n\r\nErik', '2003-04-25 16:58:48', 945, 0),
(948, 13, 'Erik Piper', 'erik@sky.cz', 'Re: Need help translating', 'One the 21nd day of the month of June in AD 1908, I baptised Jaroslav Ăron KarpiÂek, born on June 17th, 1907 to FrantiÂek KarpĂ­Âek and RĹŻÂena KavanovĂĄ (?!?!!!). His godparents were AntonĂ­n and FrantiÂek KĹĂ­Â.\r\n\r\nOn the day of June 21st, 1908, I baptised AlbĂ­n VĂĄclav KĹĂ­Â, born on March 1st, 1908, to AntonĂ­n KĹĂ­Â and FrantiÂka KĹĂ­ÂovĂĄ, born KarpĂ­ÂkovĂĄ. His godparents were VĂĄclav and AneÂka Kavan.\r\n\r\nErik', '2003-04-25 17:04:36', 946, 0),
(949, 13, 'VladimĂ­r', '', 'Re: Need help translating', '... His godparents were AntonĂ­n KĹĂ­Â and FrantiÂka (lat. Francisca) KĹĂ­ÂovĂĄ. ...', '2003-04-25 17:28:14', 948, 0),
(950, 15, 'Erik Piper', 'erik@sky.cz', 'Re: PrĂĄci?', 'All of us probably have a lot of grief awaiting us for <a href=\"http://www.internet-tips.net/Email/SPAM_spiders.htm\">posting our real email addresses here</a>, but that\'s another issue...\r\n\r\nThe \"o\" in omluvit and omlouvat is kind of hard to decipher. Generally speaking, \"o\" is easy to decipher - it works like its own shape - it\'s for motions or actions that are \"round\", \"around\", or, more abstractly, \"whole\":\r\n\r\notelefonovat lidi - to call around (\"to call-around people\")\r\nobĂ­hat - to run around\r\novlĂĄdnout - to take control over (e.g. \"ovlĂĄdnout svÄt, muahahahahaaa\")\r\nochrĂĄnit - pf. of chrĂĄnit - to successfully (\"wholly\") defend\r\nosuÂit - pf. of suÂit - to successfully (\"wholly\") dry sth. out\r\notĂĄÄet se - to turn around\r\noÂidit nÄkoho - pf. of Âidit - to successfully (\"wholly\") cheat sb.\r\nokouĹit - pf. - VULG.!! - what Monica did\r\nomĂ˝vat se - animals - to lick itself clean\r\noznĂĄmit - to announce - \"to spread known-ness (the root \"znĂĄm\") around and around\"\r\nochutnat - pf. of chutnat - to taste (the whole thing, I suppose)\r\n\r\nOmlouvat - as well as a number of other verbs - doesn\'t fit into this scheme very well. I suppose you could associate it and a number of these mystery verbs (ocitnout se, opovrhovat ÄĂ­m) with the preposition \"o\", \"about\".\r\n\r\nWatch out, there is also the harder to explain, though basically similar, root ob-.\r\n\r\nPRĂCE\r\n\r\nPrĂĄce is indeed work, and the less dignified \"job\" and the more dignified \"labo(u)r\" (as evidenced by \"HĂŠraklovy prĂĄce\" (Hercules\' Labors) and the Communist greeting \"Äest prĂĄci\'\", roughly \"May labor be honored!\" or \"Honor unto labor!\"). As in English, it also has meanings like [pronoun]\'s-workplace and [pronoun]\'s-work.\r\n\r\nSENTENCE STRUCTURE:\r\nNot much I can say besides the advice in that other post, except:\r\n- sentence structure is quirky in every language - try finding a logic in which English adverbs follow their verbs and which ones precede their verbs, for example. <i>Äest praxi, soudruhu</i>...\r\n- there\'s also the \"helper verbs and direct-object/indirect-object pronouns pile up in the \'second position in the clause,\' whatever that is, except when they don\'t\" rule:\r\nDal-jsem mu facku. (Past-tense-\'give\' past-tense-1st-p-sing-helper to-him a-slap -- I slapped him.)\r\nPĹiÂli mu ho dĂĄt (Past-tense-\'come\'-incl.-3rd-p-plural him-dative it-accusative to-give -- They came to give it to him.)\r\nNicmĂŠnÄ mÄ to mate (Nevertheless me-acc. it (\"that\")-nom. confuses -- Nevertheless, it\'s confusing for me.)\r\nPodle naÂeho nĂĄzoru mu ho dali pĹed tĂ˝dnem. (According-to our-gen. opinion-gen. him-dat. it-acc. give-past-3rd-p.-pl -- In our opinion, they gave it to him last week.)\r\n\r\nI can\'t think of except-when-they-don\'t examples right now, but I swear they\'re out there. Note the last example, where the \"second position\" doesn\'t start until the whole introductory phrase, \"in our opinion\", is over.\r\n\r\nErik', '2003-04-25 18:17:40', 944, 0),
(951, 13, 'dangerdave', 'david_sypniak@email.cz', 'polish point of view', 'well.... it all here seemed to be so cool. i finnish my high school 2day and i \r\nreally dunno what to do so i thought about learning czech language.\r\ngood idea i think, now, 2know some extra unusuall language like....czech. french and english is not enough. or.... i\'ll work on my spelling in english.\r\nbig wet kiss from southern poland.\r\na jak nie po anglicku nie umiecie to tu macie sampla moich mozliwosci po polsku\r\n. jak mozecie cos o tym jezyku ciekawego przekazac albo\r\nznacie jakies linki to piszcie na tamten czeski adres\r\nmejlmi bejbi:)', '2003-04-25 18:54:27', 0, 0),
(952, 13, 'Emil', 'zukini1@yahoo.com', 'help with small Translation (Czech to English) Thanks', 'Jak na to:\r\nPripajet tenky dratek na test-point. Pripojit dratek na 3.5V (5Vmax!!) a pripojit telefon k emidroid nebo roemmi boxu. Zapnout telefon a po konektu telefonu s boxem rychle dratek od napeti odpojit.\r\n', '2003-04-27 20:13:37', 0, 1),
(953, 13, 'Emil', 'zukini1@yahoo.com', 'Re: help with small Translation (Czech to English) Thanks', 'Pouziti:\r\nPro pod-flahovani verse CB-13-xx, pro unlock, reflash, nebo opravu founu. Po podflashovani se na displeji objevi \"phone failed see suplier\"). K oprave pouzijte flex.\r\nK oprave zmrsenyho founu budete potrebovat full flash a eeprom', '2003-04-27 20:18:39', 952, 0),
(954, 13, 'anais', 'anais7814@hotmail.com', 'aide', 'y\'a t-il quelqu\'un qui parle franĂ§ais et qui pourrait m\'aider pour apprendre &#224; parler Tch&#232;que?? ( bah, oui, ce site est cool mais je comprend pas grand chose &#224; l\'anglais). Merci d\'avance.', '2003-04-27 21:51:20', 0, 0),
(955, 13, 'Erik Piper', '', 'Re: Need help translating', 'oops, typo. Thanks for the fix.', '2003-04-28 16:21:29', 949, 0),
(956, 13, 'Erik Piper', '', 'Re: help with small Translation (Czech to English) Thanks', 'Instructions:\r\nConnect a thin wire to the test point. Connect the wire to 3.5V (5V max.!) and connect the telepohone to ??? (not a Czech word) or the ??? (not a Czech word) box. Turn on the telephone, and after it is connected to the box, quickly remove the wire from the voltage supply.', '2003-04-28 16:25:12', 952, 0),
(957, 13, 'Erik Piper', '', 'Re: help with small Translation (Czech to English) Thanks', 'Actually, considering that this is a page about cell phone hacking from a site dedicated to cell phone hacking with a forum populated by cell phone hackers, I guess I should have even answered the first one.', '2003-04-28 16:35:21', 953, 0),
(958, 13, 'Emil', 'zukini1@yahoo.com', 'Thanks  Erik', 'Usage:\r\n\r\nIn order to under-flash version CB-13-xx, for unlock, reflash or phone \r\nrepair. After underflash, \"phone failed see supplier\" message appears \r\non display. Use flex to repair.\r\n\r\nYou will need full flash and eeprom to repair damaged phone.\r\n\r\nHow to do it:\r\nsolder thin wire to test-point. connect the wire on 3.5 V (max!!!) and \r\nconnect phone to emidroid or roemmi box. switch on the phone and once \r\nthe phone connects to the box, disconnect the wire quickly from the \r\nsource.\r\n\r\n', '2003-04-28 18:20:12', 956, 0),
(959, 13, 'Krassimir', 'krkd@mail.com', 'Czech Text-to-Speach engine', 'Do You know what is TTS engine? You TYPE a word, the SB of your PC\r\n SPEAKS it. English TTS are freely downloadable from Microsoft,\r\nthey \"drive\" the so called \"MS Agent\" - little buddy in the\r\ncorner of your screen. Exists something like this for the\r\nCzech language? Where could I download it? Please help me, if you\r\nknow anything about! PROSIM !!!\r\n\r\n\r\n              Kr.K.D. Sofia, Bulgaria ', '2003-04-29 09:18:32', 0, 0),
(960, 13, 'Scott', '', 'Re: Czech Text-to-Speach engine', 'Try some of these links I found on google.com:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.pvoice.org/msagent.html\r\nhttp://www.aldostools.com/msagent.html\r\nhttp://avargas.tripod.com/msagent.html\r\n\r\nIf these do not give you what you are looking for, try going to google.com and typing in various things. e.g. TTS in Czech, Czech TTS.\r\n\r\nScott', '2003-05-01 10:51:29', 959, 0),
(961, 13, 'J', '', 'Re: Czech Text-to-Speach engine', 'http://www.pvoice.org/msagent.html.en', '2003-05-01 19:28:08', 959, 0),
(962, 13, 'Mira', 'mirathespy@hotmail.com', 'Where I put myself', 'So I have the text for this Czech song and I understand almost all of it except for one line: \"Kde jsem se tu vlastne vzal\". It definitely doesn\'t mean \"where I actually got married\". I assume \"vzit se\" means not just get married but also put yourself, as in \"put yourself into somebody else\'s shoes\", but I don\'t know how this fits into the sentence. Does it mean something like \"how I actually got here\" or \"where I actually came from\"? I know that\'s kind of a stretch...And this sort of sentence is the kind that nearly gives me aneurysms on a regular basis, with the important parts on the ends and all the little particles in the middle. I have twice as many problems with this sort of thing as I do with \"dostat\" and the imperfect and consonant clusters and adjective endings.\r\n\r\nTwo other things: what does \"kudy dal\" mean? This is from the same song (in fact, they use \"dal\" to rhyme with \"vzal\"...the rest of the song I have figured out). And where is the preposition \"u\" used, aside from the names of pubs?\r\n\r\nThank you ;)', '2003-05-05 10:15:47', 0, 0),
(963, 13, 'Krassimir', '', 'Re: Czech Text-to-Speach engine', 'Thank You very much, will try this links!\r\n                           KrKD, BG', '2003-05-07 13:14:42', 960, 0);
\r\n\r\nJakub', '2003-12-30 05:30:11', 1248, 0),
