(1172, 13, 'Stuart', 'stuartm@mailasia.com', 'Re: Czech Translation urgently needed !', 'Thanks Jana - so how would i say \'Does this meal / food contain any nuts??\'\r\n\r\nThanks in adavance, Stuart', '2003-11-03 19:02:03', 1170, 0),
(1173, 13, 'kevin', 'handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re: Czech Translation urgently needed !', 'Stuart, you need to say Nejsou v tomto jidle orechy (sorry I\'ve lost my czech keyboard) rough pronunciation is Ney-so f-tom-to jeed-le or-shek-ie You could also say Mam alergii na orechy (maam a-ler-gi-e na or-shek-ie). Avoidance of nuts in Prague is imperative ref Jakub\'s posting', '2003-11-04 02:10:08', 1172, 0),
(1174, 15, 'kevin', 'handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re: The most interesting idiom in Czech', 'Milan, I think this subject should have generated loads of replies, as a quickie I\'ll go for \"mit opici\" (hangover) though my more expert wife\'s favourite is \"liny jako prase\" aimed in my direction', '2003-11-04 02:19:03', 1158, 0),
