(1635, 13, 'Erik Piper', '', 'Re: Translation', 'Hi Jana,\r\n\r\nI have no idea how I missed this back then... I suppose your project is already done, right?\r\n\r\n[the good life]\r\n\r\nIt is the \"the\" -- it\'s a part of that idiom; just living \"a\" good life would be evocative of the idiom, but wouldn\'t really be it. (\"The good life\" googles at about 1.8 times \"a good life\", just for interest)\r\n\r\nI also can\'t think of a Czech noun phrase, but then even in English the good life is one that is most commonly *lived* anyway (to live the good life).\r\n\r\nErik', '2005-06-03 18:00:47', 1600, 0),
