(1698, 14, 'Jacek', 'alcor69_69@yahoo.com', 'I found the best calling card ever from the US to CZECH Republic', 'I have been using www.callingforcheap.com for a couple months now. \r\nI call home to the CZECH republic for  cents a minute, no connection fees/maintenance fees and nearest minute rounding! \r\n\r\nI LOVE the online account management, SPEED DIALING and NO PINS EVER!\r\n\r\nI used to go to the local convenience store to buy prepaids, but all the extra fees drove almost drove me crazy.. a 2 hour card was really worth an hourÂINSERT INTO `messages` (`id`, `board_id`, `author`, `email`, `subject`, `text`, `sent`, `following`, `send_note`) VALUES
(1724, 13, 'Kevin', 'Handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re: names', 'One of the most endearing things in czech is the total flexibility when it comes to nicknames and/or terms of endearment. If you can shorten or lengthen the name with just a small connection you\'ve got it. To my wife and daughter I can be even with my totally unczech name, Kevinka, Kevinek, Kevko, Dadko, Dadisek and more. The freedom of expression in this is a wonderful thing and although it probably is not usual to call Caroline \"Kachi\" in Czech there seem to be no absolute rules, so if it suits use it (and long may it be so). I have noticed the Slovaks often use i where the Czechs use o my wife Stana (Stanislava) is addressed in Czech as Stano but by Slovak friends as Stani. So maybe there is a Slovak connection!? \r\nSome of these pronunciations will not be as we expect in english, and have no haceks etc., but hopefully this will be enough for you to get the gist', '2005-08-04 03:10:27', 1719, 0),
(1725, 13, 'kevin', 'handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re: To Erik Piper', 'So what about you Milan why are you nosing about on a site for Czech yearner/learners, surely you should be looking at Albionca.cz if it existed', '2005-08-04 03:17:12', 1716, 0),
(1726, 13, 'Kevin', 'handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re: To Erik Piper', 'Erik how come if you are so good at languages you can\'t spell Eric', '2005-08-04 03:25:37', 1718, 0),
(1727, 14, 'Kevin', 'handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re: Is Czech food good?', 'I know what you mean, but at least theres usually a lot of it', '2005-08-04 03:33:06', 1720, 0),
(1728, 13, 'Milan Pokorny', '', 'Re: To Erik Piper', 'I am here because I want to learn something new about my mother tongue since I am a Czech teacher in Dorset UK and I really appreciate this web pages.Don\'t you want to know about English anything new as well?This pages are really brilliant.......Thanks for that', '2005-08-04 21:16:02', 1725, 1),
