(1811, 13, 'Erik Piper', '', 'Re: Jen & Pouze', 'VĂ˝jimka potvrzuje pravidlo. :-) That\'s a sense where jen isn\'t being used to mean \"only.\" No fair!\r\n\r\nAs regards the original question: pouze is seems rarer than jen to me. It also seems stronger. But I\'m not Czech (though I\'ve lived here for about a decade).\r\n\r\ne.', '2005-11-21 18:20:17', 1810, 0),
(1812, 13, 'Vlk', '', 'Re: Jen & Pouze', 'Jen poÄkej!', '2005-11-21 22:28:33', 1811, 0),
(1813, 13, 'Erik Piper', '', 'Re: Jen & Pouze', 'In short, jen can be an equivalent for the English word \"just\", whereas pouze cannot.\r\n\r\ne.', '2005-11-22 16:44:27', 1812, 0),
(1814, 13, 'Erik Piper', '', 'Re: Jen & Pouze', 'In short, jen can be an equivalent for the English word \"just\", whereas pouze cannot.\r\n\r\ne.', '2005-11-22 18:03:03', 1812, 0),
