(1819, 13, 'mike sumerlin', 'msumerlin@houston.rr.com', 'what is czech for \"Cheers\" or \"Down the Hatch\"', 'What is popular czech term for Cheers or Down the Hatch or Salute?\r\n\r\nThanks much.  For older, well-to-do worldly man.\r\nMS', '2005-12-22 08:38:44', 0, 0),
(1820, 13, 'kevin', 'handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re: what is czech for', 'Nazdravi is the word you are looking for, I think. Though I am neither well to do or worldy but I am a man and the other thing. (pronounced naz-drav-ee)', '2005-12-31 05:17:10', 1819, 0),
(1821, 15, 'kevin', 'handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re:', 'As no-one seems to have replied, I\'ll go for puzzling through with you if you like Christine. I don\'t have this Michael Heims but have a few other textbooks for reference. I too have studied on and off for last few years, not much recently though so could do with something to kickstart me again. Email if you want to take me up on this', '2005-12-31 05:25:39', 1816, 0),
(1822, 13, 'paola', 'pajpa21@yahoo.it', 'Ât\'astnĂ˝ NovĂ˝ Rok', 'Hi and a very happy new year to everybody....could any of you please translate this message \"DÄkuju za pĹĂĄnĂ­. I jĂĄ Ti pĹeju VeselĂŠ vĂĄnoce!! Moc pĹĂ­jemnĂŠ svĂĄtky a ÂÂastnĂ˝ novĂ˝ rok Do noveho roku hodne ohody, uspechu lasky a zdravi ti take preje\r\nPĹeji sluneÄnĂŠ dny\" that I received from my loved czech  friend? As I can imagine it\'s a very good wishes-message but I\'m STILL attempting to learn Cech language....many thanks and nicest regards, a Nashledanou\r\nPaola ', '2006-01-03 15:04:36', 0, 0),
