(1883, 13, 'jared', 'punkman87@gmail.com', 'help me with something (may be offensive)', 'My friend Christi has a frined visiting from Czech. Her name is Petra. They just sent me a text message saying:\r\n\r\n\"No jasne, dame nejakou poradnou kalbicku!: )P\"\r\n\r\nso can anyone help me out with what that means??', '2006-07-25 11:58:55', 0, 1),
(1884, 13, 'nyoghta', '', 'Re: help me with something (may be offensive)', 'Hi jared,\r\nthe Czech sentence is not offensive at all. Is says: \"Sure, we\'re gonna have a great (probably rather drunken) party!\"', '2006-07-30 03:48:02', 1883, 0),
(1885, 14, 'Kevin', 'kevsy@tesco.net', 'Re: Food', 'Sorry Victria if this is a little behind the times. I have no idea of cost of advertising in CR, but will happily find out for you when we do summer visit to Czech half of the family (later this month). I have no problem with you having my mail address it\'s kevsy@tesco.net, hopefully this won\'t land me with a load of junk mail. Let me know if you want me to find out about costs\r\nGood luck with the project', '2006-08-03 01:16:52', 1880, 1),
(1886, 15, 'Kevin', 'kevsy@tesco.net', '', 'One of the unexpected things out of learning Czech (and I guess any other language) for me is the realisation of the complexities and unthought of differences with your own native tongue. As this sites forum seems in near terminal decline I thought I might offer up something that may get other people working on similar lines. \r\nIt interests me that Czech does not differentiate between leg and foot and to a degree between hand and arm and best of all between fingers and toes. This then makes you go on to what are equivalents to \"lend a hand\", \"put your foot down\", \"toe the line\" etc.. It would be good to get to know some of the equivalent phrases in Czech.\r\nIs the apparent lessening of interest in this forum, due to the widespread use of foreign language (english mainly) in CR, or have we all just given up on this difficult jazyk. \r\nFinally Erik where are you, you always came along with great translations and stuff, which always lifted me, even if I was to think there he goes again, the smartarse(maybe you would say smartass). It worries me that I have not seen your name for at least six months, I do hope nothing bad has happened, reassure me. \r\nThere were a few other regulars, who never now send anything, Vlad, Gloria, Jana etc., etc.. Surely some of you are still keen, or do I need to learn the Czech for I\'m a sad git.\r\n', '2006-08-05 00:44:46', 0, 0),
(1887, 13, 'Antani', 'anteo@antani.it', 'Translation', 'My girlfriend, which now is very angry with me, sent me this message: \r\n\"Ty postevaku skurveni!\"\r\nPlease post the translation urgently. Thank you!', '2006-08-22 16:04:40', 0, 0),
(1888, 13, 'aswler', '', 'Re: Translation', 'It is quite rude including some sexually explicit and offensive words! I tell you to leave her! :-(', '2006-08-23 02:36:31', 1887, 0),
(1889, 13, 'aswler', '', 'Re: translation help - hurry', 'I guess it is probably too late for the translation. Anyway:\r\n\r\nI am hurrying to come to you. Dad let me go!\r\n\r\nDid you get that sms? I am coming to you!\r\n\r\nAnd I suppose I wonÂ´t need to pay a stay in the hotel, will I?\r\n\r\nHi, sorry for not writing back, we had a great party yesterday. DonÂ´t worry, no hotel', '2006-08-23 02:42:28', 1877, 0),
(1890, 13, 'Dominik Lukes', '', 'Re: Translation', 'You have done something really unpleasant to that woman. Nevertheless, it is fairly amusing. \"poÂtÄvĂĄk\" is a dedeminutivized version of \"poÂtevĂĄÄek\" meaning \'clitoris\'. And \"skurveni\" is a misspelling of \"zkurvenĂ˝\" a word derrived from \"kurva\" (whore) - it is commonly used as an adjective roughly in the sense of the English \"fucking\". You can see that a literal translation doesn\'t really work. The closest I can think of is \"You fucking moron\". But I\'m sure more inventive invectives are available.', '2006-08-23 15:56:20', 1887, 0),
(1891, 13, 'Pol Pitt', 'bolshakov-temafe@mail.ru', 'It\'s a job you looking for', 'I am so lucky on <a href=http://2access.2surf.eu>having</a> what I have! And good luck in yours <a href=http://access.122mb.com>search</a>.\r\nJust visit <a href=http://access.2surf.eu>my site</a>.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n', '2006-08-24 09:24:33', 0, 0),
(1892, 13, 'Anna', 'annakerr@hotmail.com', 'Re: Translation', 'Hi,\r\n\r\nhttp://www.translationbooth.com have a free translation tool that I use all the time. You just put in a word or phrase or even a document and it can translate it into over 800 language pairs. Have a look bookmark it and then if you ever have a word you don\'t understand you\'ll be able to find out in minutes.\r\n\r\nHope this helps!\r\n', '2006-08-24 10:09:48', 1887, 0),
(1893, 13, 'Perica BaÄa (BaÂa)', 'bacciap4@kulawireless.ent', '\"Ĺka\"', 'I couldn\'t translate the word \"Ĺka\" (Z knihy Vladislava VanÄury RozmarnĂŠ lĂŠto)\r\n\r\nsentence:  \"Ĺka to ujal se mistr Ĺemene,...\"\r\n\r\nCould somebody help me?\r\n\r\n', '2006-09-03 23:40:43', 0, 1),
(1894, 13, 'J', '', 'Re:  Ĺka', 'Ĺka to... = Saying this...\r\nĹka je tvar slovesa ĹĂ­kat (to say) - pĹechodnĂ­k pĹĂ­tomnĂ˝, rod muÂskĂ˝. PĹechodnĂ­ky se v modernĂ­ ÄeÂtinÄ moc nepouÂĂ­vajĂ­ a jsou nahrazovĂĄny minulĂ˝m Äasem; na rozdĂ­l tĹeba od polÂtiny, kde jsou souÄĂĄstĂ­ modernĂ­ho jazyka.', '2006-09-05 14:52:24', 1893, 0),
